title: Karen_PriceComplaint_EN
---
Karen: Excuse me! Can you explain why this product costs more here than it does on the website?

Karen: I shouldn't have to pay more just because I came to the actual store!

-> Explain the price difference
    Player: Sometimes online prices have different promotions than the ones in the store.
    Karen: So I have to buy it online while I'm literally standing in front of the product?
    <<if get_sanity() >= 50>>
        Karen: This is ridiculous! I want to speak to someone who can actually do something about this!
        <<add_stress 20>>
        <<jump Karen_PriceEscalation_EN>>
    <<else>>
        <<add_stress 8>>
        Karen: Well... I'm not happy about it, but I suppose that makes sense.
        <<jump Karen_PriceResolved_EN>>
    <<endif>>

-> Offer to check the price
    Player: Let me check if we can match the online price.
    <<add_stress 5>>
    Karen: You'd better. I'm not paying extra for something that costs less online.
    <<jump Karen_PriceResolved_EN>>

-> Tell her to buy it online
    Player: If you want the online price, you can purchase it directly from the website.
    <<add_stress 20>>
    Karen: Are you telling me to do your job from my phone?
    <<jump Karen_PriceEscalation_EN>>
===

title: Karen_PriceResolved_EN
---
Karen: Fine. Thank you for checking the price.

Karen: Although I still think the store should make this easier.
===

title: Karen_PriceEscalation_EN
---
Karen: I want to speak to the manager!

Karen: And I hope they can explain why a website has more power than the employees.
===

title: Karen_DirtyFloor_EN
---
Karen: Excuse me! Do you work here?

Player: Yes. Can I help you?

Karen: There's a small stain on the floor, and I've spent five minutes trying not to step on it.

-> Apologize and clean it
    Player: I'm sorry. I'll take care of it right now.
    <<add_stress 5>>
    Karen: Thank you. Finally, someone is paying attention.
    <<jump Karen_FloorResolved_EN>>

-> Explain that someone will clean it
    Player: We've already reported it. Someone should be here soon.
    <<add_stress 12>>
    Karen: "Soon" isn't a time. When exactly?
    <<jump Karen_FloorEscalation_EN>>

-> Ignore the complaint
    <<add_stress 20>>
    Karen: Unbelievable! Do I have to clean the floor myself?
    <<jump Karen_FloorEscalation_EN>>
===

title: Karen_FloorResolved_EN
---
Karen: Much better.

Karen: I don't know how such a small stain turned into such a big problem.
===

title: Karen_FloorEscalation_EN
---
Karen: This is a SAFETY issue.

Karen: I'm going to leave a review about this.
===

title: Karen_CouponComplaint_EN
---
Karen: Excuse me! This coupon says I get a discount, but the system won't accept it.

Player: Let me take a look.

Karen: I already looked at it. It clearly says "valid in store."

-> Check the coupon
    Player: I'll check the terms and see what's going on.
    <<add_stress 5>>
    Karen: Good. That's exactly what I expected someone to do.
    <<jump Karen_CouponResolved_EN>>

-> Explain that it may have restrictions
    Player: It might have some restrictions or an expiration date.
    <<if get_sanity() >= 50>>
        Karen: I don't need an explanation! I need it to WORK!
        <<add_stress 18>>
        <<jump Karen_CouponEscalation_EN>>
    <<else>>
        Karen: Hmph. Then check it.
        <<add_stress 8>>
        <<jump Karen_CouponResolved_EN>>
    <<endif>>

-> Tell her to read the terms
    Player: Maybe we should check the fine print on the coupon.
    <<add_stress 15>>
    Karen: Are you saying I can't read?
    <<jump Karen_CouponEscalation_EN>>
===

title: Karen_CouponResolved_EN
---
Karen: Oh. I see.

Karen: Well, thank you for explaining it.
===

title: Karen_CouponEscalation_EN
---
Karen: This shouldn't be this complicated!

Karen: I'm going to speak to the manager.
===

title: Karen_BrokenDisplay_EN
---
Karen: Excuse me! Who is supposed to fix this?

Player: What's wrong?

Karen: This sign is crooked. I've been looking at it since I walked in!

-> Fix the sign
    Player: You're right. Let me straighten it out.
    <<add_stress 5>>
    Karen: Much better. Thank you.
    <<jump Karen_DisplayResolved_EN>>

-> Say it isn't important
    Player: I don't think it really affects the purchase.
    <<add_stress 15>>
    Karen: It's not about the purchase! It's about how the store looks!
    <<jump Karen_DisplayEscalation_EN>>

-> Say you'll report it
    Player: I'll report it so maintenance can fix it.
    <<add_stress 8>>
    Karen: Fine. I hope it doesn't take a week.
    <<jump Karen_DisplayResolved_EN>>
===

title: Karen_DisplayResolved_EN
---
Karen: Thank you.

Karen: Now it looks like a professional store again.
===

title: Karen_DisplayEscalation_EN
---
Karen: If customers have to fix the store's presentation themselves, we have a serious problem.

Karen: I want to speak to the manager.
===
